# ===== Stage Editor top menu (Adobe style) =====
# ===== Menu titles =====
menu_stage => Stage
menu_object => Object
menu_camera => Camera
menu_view => View
menu_file => File
menu_help => Help

# ===== Status bar =====
status_stage => Stage:
status_directory => Dir:
status_object => Object:
status_pos => Pos:
status_zoom => Zoom:

# ===== Items: Stage menu =====
item_stage_select => Stage
item_reload_stage => Reload Stage
item_load_template => Load Template
item_directory => Asset Directory
item_hide_gf => Hide Girlfriend
item_default_zoom => Default Zoom
item_cam_speed => Camera Speed
label_stage_select => Stage:
label_directory => Directory:
label_default_zoom => Default Zoom:
label_cam_speed => Camera Speed:
desc_stage_select => Select the stage to edit. Switching stages rebuilds the editor (stability first).
desc_reload_stage => Reload the current stage JSON and background from disk.
desc_load_template => Replace current stage data with a blank template.
desc_directory => Asset directory for this stage (e.g. week1 / week4), decides which week folder loads images.
desc_hide_gf => Hide the girlfriend character on stage.
desc_default_zoom => Default camera zoom for this stage.
desc_cam_speed => Camera follow speed multiplier.

# ===== Items: Object menu =====
label_obj_name => Name:
label_obj_type => Type:
label_obj_image => Image:
label_obj_pos => Position:
label_obj_scale => Scale:
label_obj_alpha => Alpha:
label_obj_angle => Angle:
item_obj_new_sprite => New Sprite (Image)
item_obj_new_animated => New Animated Sprite
item_obj_new_square => New Solid Color
item_obj_delete => Delete Object
item_obj_duplicate => Duplicate Object
item_obj_anim => Open Animation Editor
item_obj_move_up => Move Up a Layer
item_obj_move_down => Move Down a Layer
desc_obj_name => Name of the currently selected object (for Lua/HScript).
desc_obj_type => Type of the selected object (sprite / animatedSprite / square / character).
desc_obj_image => Image asset used by the selected object.
desc_obj_pos => X / Y position of the selected object.
desc_obj_scale => X / Y scale of the selected object.
desc_obj_alpha => Opacity of the selected object (0% - 100%).
desc_obj_angle => Rotation angle of the selected object.
desc_obj_new_sprite => Pick an image from the images/ folder to create a plain sprite.
desc_obj_new_animated => Pick a sprite with an XML/JSON/TXT animation file from images/.
desc_obj_new_square => Create a 200x200 solid color block.
desc_obj_delete => Delete the selected background object (characters can't be deleted).
desc_obj_duplicate => Duplicate the selected object and insert it into the list.
desc_obj_anim => Open the animation editor substate to edit frames/offsets.
desc_obj_move_up => Move the selected object one layer up in the render order.
desc_obj_move_down => Move the selected object one layer down in the render order.
item_show_bf => Show Player (BF)
item_show_dad => Show Opponent (Opp)
item_show_gf => Show Girlfriend (GF)
desc_show_bf => Show or hide the Boyfriend character.
desc_show_dad => Show or hide the Opponent character.
desc_show_gf => Show or hide the Girlfriend character (syncs Hide Girlfriend data).
desc_obj_list_item => Click to select this object (syncs with W/S selection).

# ===== Items: Camera menu =====
label_cam_zoom => Zoom:
label_cam_target => Target:
label_cam_bf_x => Player X:
label_cam_bf_y => Player Y:
label_cam_dad_x => Opponent X:
label_cam_dad_y => Opponent Y:
label_cam_gf_x => Girlfriend X:
label_cam_gf_y => Girlfriend Y:
desc_cam_zoom => Current camera zoom (applies live while editing).
desc_cam_target => Camera follow target (player / opponent / girlfriend).
desc_cam_offset => Camera offset when focusing that character.

# ===== Items: View menu =====
item_low_quality => Show Low Quality Sprites
item_high_quality => Show High Quality Sprites
item_toggle_help => Toggle Help
item_focus_bf => Focus Player
item_focus_dad => Focus Opponent
item_focus_gf => Focus Girlfriend
desc_low_quality => Show background sprites marked as low quality.
desc_high_quality => Show background sprites marked as high quality.
desc_toggle_help => Show or hide the shortcut help overlay.
desc_focus_bf => Move camera to the player character.
desc_focus_dad => Move camera to the opponent character.
desc_focus_gf => Move camera to the girlfriend character.

# ===== Items: File menu =====
item_save => Save
desc_save => Save the current stage JSON (objects and camera data) to a file.

# ===== Help menu =====
help_camera => Navigation
item_tutorial => Tutorial
desc_tutorial => Open the beginner tutorial: stage background setup, importing assets, saving, etc.
help_cam_zoom => Q / E - Zoom out / in
help_cam_move => J / K / L / I - Move camera
help_cam_reset => R - Reset zoom
desc_help_camera => Camera navigation: Q/E zoom, J/K/L/I move, R reset.
desc_help_cam_zoom => Q / E - zoom the camera out / in.
desc_help_cam_move => J / K / L / I - move the camera.
desc_help_cam_reset => R - reset camera zoom to the stage default.
help_obj => Object Controls
help_obj_move => Arrow keys - Move selected object
help_obj_sel => W / S - Switch selection
help_obj_scale => Shift - 4x movement
desc_help_obj => Object editing: arrow keys move, W/S switch selection.
desc_help_obj_move => Arrow keys - move the selected object in 5px steps.
desc_help_obj_sel => W / S - switch selection in the object list.
desc_help_obj_scale => Hold Shift - movement steps become 4x.
help_other => Other
help_other_shift => Shift - Speed up
help_other_help => F7 - Help
help_other_exit => Esc - Back to menu
desc_help_other => Other common actions.
desc_help_other_shift => Hold Shift - speed up camera/object movement.
desc_help_other_help => F7 - show or hide the help overlay.
desc_help_other_exit => Esc - exit the editor back to the main menu.
